{
  "unit": {
    "id": "9",
    "title": "Tomorrow I will…",
    "blurb": "The future tense in every person",
    "intro": "The future tense says what will happen. For -āre and -ēre verbs it uses -bō, -bis, -bit, -bimus, -bitis, -bunt: _amābō_ (I will love), _habēbō_ (I will have). For -ere and -īre verbs the endings are -am, -ēs, -et, -ēmus, -ētis, -ent: _edam_ (I will eat), _audiam_ (I will hear). A time word like _crās_ (tomorrow) or _mox_ (soon) comes along to confirm it."
  },
